        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: J. I. Clements Stadium, Statesboro, Bulloch County, Georgia, United States\n- Organizations: Georgia Southern University, Georgia Southern Eagles baseball team, Sun Belt Conference\n- People: Garland T. Byrd\n- Roles: Lieutenant Governor of Georgia\n- Topics: college baseball\n\nFacts:\n- Garland T. Byrd was born on July 16, 1924, and died on June 1, 1997.\n- Garland T. Byrd was a Democratic politician from Georgia in the United States.\n- Garland T. Byrd served as the fourth Lieutenant Governor of Georgia from 1959 to 1963.\n- Statesboro is the largest city in Bulloch County, Georgia, and it is the county seat of Bulloch County.\n- Statesboro is located in the southeastern part of the state of Georgia in the United States.\n- J. I. Clements Stadium is a baseball venue in Statesboro, Georgia, United States.\n- J. I. Clements Stadium is the home venue of the Georgia Southern University Eagles college baseball team in the Division I Sun Belt Conference.\n- The 2017 Georgia Southern Eagles baseball team played its home games at J. I. Clements Stadium.",
